{"t": 1794106743.8324313, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` computed its offset as `number * size`, so a 1-based `?page=1` request returned the second page. The offset is now `(number - 1) * size`, matching the API's documented 1-based page numbering.\n\nVerified locally:\n- page(items, 1, 3) -> [1, 2, 3]\n- page(items, 2, 3) -> [4, 5, 6]\n- page(items, 4, 3) -> [10] for 10 items\n- page(items, 5, 3) -> [] (past the end)", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix page() to treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)"}, "ok": true}
